Atlas overlay patch 0124: fed/fed-omnibox
Why: a Federate name typed in the address bar or the new tab page's field (home.fed, lobo.pagina, an http(s)
 spelling of one) was classified as a search: the 23 Federate TLDs are not in the engine's registry data, so
 AutocompleteInput::Parse() answered UNKNOWN ("foo.xxx: Chrome won't know it is a real URL") and the default
 match was the search provider. The name left the machine (search request, suggest requests while typing) and
 the page the person wanted did not open (QA-A9-WEB-ATLAS-1, lead rule: a Federate name never reaches the web).
 Now (1) Parse() turns an input whose host ends in a known Federate TLD into a URL whose canonical form is the
 fed:// address (atlas_fed::MapHttpToFed, the same function the loaders use); (2) SearchProvider::Start()
 stops for such an input, so no suggest request and no search match is made for it ("?home.fed" still
 searches). The TLD list is ONE definition in components/atlas_fed_tlds, read by the omnibox and by the fed
 area (chrome/browser/atlas/fed/fed_url.h forwards to it). The new tab page needs no hook: its field uses the
 same classifier (and newtab_handler.cc opens a Federate name directly, before asking it).
Files: components/omnibox/browser/autocomplete_input.cc, components/omnibox/browser/search_provider.cc, components/omnibox/browser/BUILD.gn
Test filter: *AtlasFedOmnibox*; journey: type lobo.pagina in the address bar and the new tab field, Enter: fed://lobo.pagina opens, no request to the search provider
Rebase risk: M (one early return in Parse(), one early return in SearchProvider::Start(), one include and one dependency each)
Release: 0.13
License: GPL-3.0-or-later (hunks in files the inherited series patches)
Verified at: 156.0.8078.79, base tree plus the patches before it in the series (dev slot 4)

